question:
Study the code below. What does `display: flex` do to the `<nav>` element?

[css code]
nav {
  display: flex;
}

Study the code below. Which property changes the paragraph to use the Arial font?

[css code]
p {
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
}

Study the code below. Which attribute tells the browser where to find the image file?

[html code]
&lt;img src="logo.png" alt="Company logo"&gt;

Study the code below. What does the `transform` declaration do?

[css code]
.card {
  transform: translateX(20px);
}

Study the code below. Which statement best describes the effect of `position: relative`?

[css code]
.badge {
  position: relative;
  top: 5px;
}

Study the code below. Which property changes the paragraph’s text to blue?

[css code]
p {
  color: blue;
}

Study the code below. Which property creates 20 pixels of space inside the box?

[css code]
.box {
  padding: 20px;
}

Study the code below. Which property controls whether `.front` appears above `.back`?

[css code]
.front {
  position: relative;
  z-index: 2;
}

.back {
  position: relative;
  z-index: 1;
}

Study the code below. Which part defines the stages of the animation?

[css code]
@keyframes fadeIn {
  from { opacity: 0; }
  to { opacity: 1; }
}

Study the code below. Which property makes the animation last 2 seconds for one cycle?

[css code]
.box {
  animation-name: slide;
  animation-duration: 2s;
}

Study the code below. Which element inserts the image into the webpage?

[html code]
&lt;img src="photo.jpg" alt="A mountain landscape"&gt;

Study the code below. Which property centers the flex items along the horizontal main axis?

[css code]
.container {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: center;
}

Study the code below. What will happen when the button’s background color changes?

[css code]
button {
  background-color: blue;
  transition: background-color 0.5s;
}

button:hover {
  background-color: green;
}
